{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 2 Time complexity / Estimating efficiency","source_pages":"27-31","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"complexity","bridge":"complexity_fit","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"先看输入规模，再用时间复杂度估算总操作量。如果两层循环会把规模乘起来，量级很快就会超出时限。","teaching_value":"适合把“先看规模再定方法”讲成学生能落笔估算的一步。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/basic/complexity.md","chapter_or_section":"时间复杂度 / 定义","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"complexity","bridge":"complexity_fit","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：先背一个更高级的方法名就算想清楚了。真正先要估的是总操作量会不会先炸。","teaching_value":"适合把复杂度桥的常见误解先破掉。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 2 Time complexity / Estimating efficiency","source_pages":"27-31","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"complexity","bridge":"complexity_fit","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如 `N=50000`、`M=50000` 时，双层枚举就是 `50000×50000` 次，这一步光总量级就已经很危险了。","teaching_value":"适合让学生先拿纸笔估一次总量级。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 3 Binary search","source_pages":"41-43","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"left_bound_update","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"在有序数组里找边界，不是只问“有没有这个值”，而是问“最左边那个满足条件的位置在哪里”。因此一旦中点已经满足条件，不能急着丢掉它，而要继续保留它作为候选。","teaching_value":"适合解释为什么 a[mid] == x 时还要保留 mid，而不是直接跳到 mid 的右边。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/basic/binary.md","chapter_or_section":"二分法 / 过程","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"left_bound_update","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：`a[mid] == x` 就说明这题做完了。真正要站稳的是：找最左位置时，mid 还只是候选，不能立刻丢掉。","teaching_value":"适合把左边界桥的误区讲透。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 3 Binary search","source_pages":"41-43","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"left_bound_update","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"数组 `[1,2,2,2,3]` 里找最左边的 `2`，如果 `mid` 落在中间那个 `2`，你还得保留它继续往左缩。","teaching_value":"适合让学生立刻看到“保留 mid”的必要性。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/basic/binary.md","chapter_or_section":"最大值最小化","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"check_condition","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"二分答案不是直接在答案区间里乱猜，而是先把“某个值可不可行”这件事单独判断清楚。只要可行性随答案变化保持单调，就可以用二分去找边界。","teaching_value":"适合把判定函数的职责和单调性讲清楚。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/basic/binary.md","chapter_or_section":"最大值最小化","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"check_condition","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：`check(mid)` 在直接算答案。真正要站稳的是：它只回答“当前这个 mid 可不可行”。","teaching_value":"适合把 check 的职责钉死在“可行性判断”上。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 3 Binary search","source_pages":"41-43","topic_l1":"basic","topic_l2":"binary_search","bridge":"check_condition","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如 `check(5)=true`，它只说明“当前要求最小值至少为 5 这件事还能做到”，不是说最终答案就等于 5。","teaching_value":"适合把返回值语义讲成一句能落笔的话。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 7 Dynamic programming / Recursive formulation","source_pages":"75-78","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"state_design","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"动态规划先要把“一个状态到底在回答什么小问题”说清楚。只有状态含义先站稳，后面才知道这个状态应该依赖哪些更小的状态。","teaching_value":"适合把“状态格里存什么”从代码变量层，拉回子问题语义层。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/dp/basic.md","chapter_or_section":"动态规划基本思想","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"state_design","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：状态就是随手起的变量名。真正要站稳的是：状态在回答哪个子问题、存的是哪个子问题的结果。","teaching_value":"适合打掉状态层最常见的抽象误会。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 7 Dynamic programming / Recursive formulation","source_pages":"75-78","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"state_design","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如 `dp[x][y]` 不是“整题答案放哪”，而是“站在格子 `(x,y)` 这个状态上，子问题的最优结果是多少”。","teaching_value":"适合让学生把状态语义和代码位置对应起来。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 7 Dynamic programming / Recursive formulation","source_pages":"76-78","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"transition_design","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"先确定当前状态的含义，再看“第一步可以怎么选”或“当前状态能从哪些更小状态转来”。转移式不是凭感觉写出来的，而是由这些更小子问题拼起来的。","teaching_value":"适合解释为什么写转移前要先把来源想全。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/dp/basic.md","chapter_or_section":"动态规划基本思想","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"transition_design","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：转移式像是凭感觉试出来的。真正要站稳的是：当前状态必须先看清能从哪些更小状态转来。","teaching_value":"适合把“转移凭感觉”这个误解先破掉。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Chapter 7 Dynamic programming / Recursive formulation","source_pages":"76-78","topic_l1":"dp","topic_l2":"dp_basic","bridge":"transition_design","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如数字三角形里当前格，不是随便从上面来，而是先比较“左上来源”和“右上来源”这两类更小状态。","teaching_value":"适合让学生先把来源分类看全。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/string/trie.md","chapter_or_section":"定义 / 引入","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"method_selection","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"题目里如果有很多字符串，而且问题反复围绕前缀关系展开，就要警惕：这些相同开头能不能先合在一起看。这个信号通常比“我感觉要用 trie”更可靠。","teaching_value":"适合把 trie 的方法选择桥讲成题面信号，而不是题感。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/string/trie.md","chapter_or_section":"定义 / 引入","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"method_selection","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：以前做过类似题，所以这题也一定是 trie。真正更可靠的是：题面里有没有“很多字符串 + 反复前缀关系”这个信号。","teaching_value":"适合把方法选择从题感拉回题面信号。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Trie structure","source_pages":"254-255","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"method_selection","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如消息有 `101`、`100`、`11`，而查询一直在问前缀关系，这时“前两条前面两位一样”就是支持 trie 的直接信号。","teaching_value":"适合让学生先抓到支持 trie 的那个最小信号。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Trie structure","source_pages":"254-255","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"shared_prefix_merging","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"如果很多字符串有相同前缀，它们在 trie 里会先共用一段路径。这样查询时，不需要把所有字符串重新逐个看一遍，而是沿当前前缀那条路径往下走。","teaching_value":"适合把“公共前缀为什么值得先合起来看”讲清楚。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Trie structure","source_pages":"254-255","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"shared_prefix_merging","snippet_type":"algorithm_overview","excerpt":"Trie 的作用不是背答案，而是把字符串集合按前缀组织起来。查询、找最长前缀、统计某个前缀下有多少字符串，都会回到“沿前缀路径走”这件事。","teaching_value":"适合补“这一步在整套方法里负责什么”。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/string/trie.md","chapter_or_section":"定义 / 引入","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"shared_prefix_merging","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：trie 像把答案神奇背出来了。真正要站稳的是：它只是把相同前缀先合在一起，所以查询时能沿路径走。","teaching_value":"适合先破掉 trie 的“魔法答案表”误解。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Trie structure","source_pages":"254-255","topic_l1":"string","topic_l2":"trie","bridge":"shared_prefix_merging","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如消息有 `101`、`100`、`11`，前两条都会经过前缀 `10` 这个节点，所以这里既能讲“共享前缀”，也能讲“经过次数至少是 2”。","teaching_value":"适合让机制桥和节点计数语义在一个最小例子里合起来。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/ds/seg.md","chapter_or_section":"引入 / 基本结构与建树","topic_l1":"data_structure","topic_l2":"segment_tree","bridge":"lazy_semantics","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"线段树节点维护的是一整段区间的信息。lazy 不是“代码还没执行完”，而是“这段区间已经确定要加上这笔更新，但还没往两个孩子分下去”。","teaching_value":"适合把 lazy 标记的语义讲清楚。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/ds/seg.md","chapter_or_section":"引入 / 基本结构与建树","topic_l1":"data_structure","topic_l2":"segment_tree","bridge":"lazy_semantics","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"最容易误会的是：lazy 只是“代码没跑完”。真正要站稳的是：lazy 记录的是这段区间还欠给孩子的那份更新信息。","teaching_value":"适合把 lazy 的语义误解先纠正。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"cp-pdf","source_title":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","source_file":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook.pdf","chapter_or_section":"Range queries / Segment tree","source_pages":"161-166","topic_l1":"data_structure","topic_l2":"segment_tree","bridge":"lazy_semantics","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"比如节点管 `[1,4]`，`lazy=3` 表示这段区间每个数都还欠着 `+3` 没下传；如果左儿子长度是 `2`，pushdown 时左儿子的 `sum` 会先加 `3×2`。","teaching_value":"适合把 lazy 讲成一个能手算的小例子。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/graph/lca.md","chapter_or_section":"最近公共祖先 / 树上路径","topic_l1":"graph","topic_l2":"tree_path_difference","bridge":"tree_path_difference","snippet_type":"bridge_explanation","excerpt":"树上两点之间的路径可以先用 LCA 找到分叉点。做多条路径贡献统计时，不要每次沿整条路径逐点加，而是先在端点和 LCA 附近做差分标记。","teaching_value":"适合把 P3128 的树剖 LCA + 差分讲成路径贡献桥。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/graph/lca.md","chapter_or_section":"最近公共祖先 / 树上路径","topic_l1":"graph","topic_l2":"tree_path_difference","bridge":"tree_path_difference","snippet_type":"misconception","excerpt":"求出 LCA 或写了树剖，不等于经过次数会自动出现。真正要站稳的是：LCA 只定位路径，贡献还要靠差分标记和 DFS 汇总还原。","teaching_value":"适合破掉“方法名等于解法”的误解。","needs_manual_review":false}
{"source_family":"oi-wiki","source_title":"OI Wiki","source_file":"docs/graph/lca.md","chapter_or_section":"最近公共祖先 / 树上路径","topic_l1":"graph","topic_l2":"tree_path_difference","bridge":"tree_path_difference","snippet_type":"mini_example","excerpt":"只看一条路径 s 到 t：先让 s 和 t 各加一，再在 lca 和 parent(lca) 附近抵消，最后 DFS 向上汇总，就能把贡献落回路径上的点。","teaching_value":"适合给树上差分知识卡补一个可手算的小板书。","needs_manual_review":false}
